# General C++20 Standards

## Naming
- Variables and functions: `snake_case`
- Classes and structs: `PascalCase`
- Constants and macros: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Private members: `m_` prefix (e.g. `m_baud`, `m_device`)

## Memory and Ownership
- No raw owning pointers — use `std::unique_ptr` or `std::shared_ptr`
- No raw `new` / `delete` — prefer factory functions or `std::make_unique`
- RAII for all resources (file descriptors, serial ports, Qt objects)

```cpp
// ❌ BAD
IComms* comms = new SerialCommsPosix(device, baud);

// ✅ GOOD
auto comms = std::make_unique<SerialCommsPosix>(device, baud);
```

## Documentation
- All public functions and classes must have a Doxygen `/** @brief */` comment
- Comments explain *why*, not *what* — do not narrate the code

## Commit hygiene
- No `TODO` or `FIXME` in committed code — open a GitHub Issue instead
- No secrets, hard-coded device paths, or credentials
- Match `#include` ordering and paths from neighboring files before adding new ones
